          "description": "TERRAIN-FOLLOWING (rank-3) control thicknesses from a THREE-DIMENSIONAL edge array: lev_thickness_3d[gi,gj,gk] = pe[gi,gj,gk+1] - pe[gi,gj,gk] over [lon, lat, lev], gathering the [lon, lat, lev_nodes] edge array pe. This is the Psurf-coupled hybrid-sigma-pressure counterpart of lev_thickness: a consuming model builds a 3-D pressure-at-edges pe[i,j,kn] = Ap[kn] + Bp[kn]*Ps(i,j,t) (which varies in longitude, latitude and time whenever the surface pressure does) and applies this template to define its [lon,lat,lev]-shaped `dp` observed (positive when pe increases with the lev index — the required orientation). The physical `dp` is the reconstruction width consumed by the terrain-following flux-form vertical operators (ppm_flux_D_lev_mono_hybrid_noflux_bc). Aggregation indices gi/gj/gk (distinct from a rule's i/j/k) for the non-hygienic-inlining reason documented on lev_center and lev_thickness.",
